{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs28\b\cf1 WorkMonitor Project Concepts Documentation\par\pard\fs22\b0\par This document explains the main concepts, technologies, and modules used in this HR Management project. It is written in a Word-compatible RTF format so it can be opened in Microsoft Word and exported to PDF if needed.\par\pard\par\b 1. Project Overview\b0\par This project is an employee management and HR operations system built with Next.js. It helps manage employees, attendance, tasks, leave requests, expenses, notifications, payroll, and reports. The application is designed for three roles: admin, HR, and employee.\par\par\b 2. Main Technologies Used\b0\par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - Next.js 16: full-stack React framework used for routing, server components, API routes, and app structure.\par - React 19: component-based user interface library.\par - TypeScript: adds static typing and safer code.\par - Tailwind CSS: utility-first styling system.\par - shadcn/ui and Radix UI: reusable accessible UI components.\par - MongoDB + Mongoose: database and schema-based modeling.\par - Cloudinary: image upload and media hosting.\par - PDFKit: used for generating salary slip PDFs.\par - Zod: validation library.\par - React Hook Form: forms and validation.\par - Lucide React: icons.\par\pard\par\b 3. Project Structure\b0\par The project is organized into sections such as: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - src/app: app routes, pages, API endpoints, login flow, and server-side actions\par - src/components: reusable UI components like headers, tables, and layout\par - src/lib: shared logic and helper modules such as authentication, database connection, payroll calculations, store, and config\par - src/models: Mongoose schema definitions\par - src/hooks: reusable hooks like data table and search logic\par - src/styles.css: global theme styling\par\pard\par\b 4. App Router and Page Flow\b0\par The app uses the Next.js App Router. The main routes are inside src/app and include: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - /login: sign-in page\par - /dashboard: overview screen\par - /employees: employee listing and management\par - /attendance: attendance tracking\par - /tasks: employee task assignment\par - /leaves: leave request and approval flow\par - /expenses: expense requests and review\par - /salary-slips: payroll and payslip generation\par - /holidays: holiday calendar\par - /reports: summaries and analytical views\par - /notifications: system alerts\par - /profile: employee information and image upload\par - /settings: configurations\par\pard\par\b 5. Authentication and Authorization\b0\par Authentication is handled by loginAction() in src/app/actions.ts. The user enters a username or email and password. The backend checks:\par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - admin credentials from environment variables\par - HR credentials from environment variables\par - employee credentials stored in the Employee collection\par\pard\par After successful login, the user data is stored in localStorage under the key ems_auth_v1. The application reads the current user using getCurrentUser().\par\par Role-based authorization is implemented using the Role type: admin, hr, employee. The ROLE_MENUS object defines which pages each role can access. This is the core concept behind access control in the project.\par\par\b 6. State Management\b0\par This project does not use Redux. Instead, it uses a lightweight custom store pattern in src/lib/store.ts.\par\par Concepts used: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - localStorage session storage for authentication state\par - useSyncExternalStore for reactive database-like state updates\par - custom listener system to re-render components when data changes\par - useDB() hook to fetch and monitor the employee database state\par - useGlobalSearch() for global search state\par\pard\par This is a simple but effective pattern for small-to-medium internal business applications.\par\par\b 7. Database and Mongoose Models\b0\par MongoDB is the database used. Mongoose schemas model each object. The database connection file src/lib/mongoose.ts connects to MongoDB using MONGO_URI from the environment.\par\par Important models: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - Employee: employee personal information and employment details\par - Task: task assignment, status, progress, reviews, comments\par - Attendance: login/logout records, working time, productivity\par - Leave: leave types, dates, review status, comments\par - Expense: reimbursement requests with approval status\par - Notification: alerts sent to users\par - Holiday: company holiday definitions\par - SalarySlip: payroll data and payslip details\par - Setting: system configuration like maintenance mode\par\pard\par These models define the shapes of the records and enforce validation rules.\par\par\b 8. Server Actions and API Routes\b0\par The project combines Server Actions and route handlers.\par\par Server actions are implemented in src/app/actions.ts for operations such as:\par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - login\par - employee creation and management\par - task creation and review\par - leave approval and rejection\par - expense review and reimbursement\par - notification sending and reading\par - holiday maintenance\par - payroll generation\par\pard\par API routes in src/app/api/ are used for endpoints like attendance, reports, salary slips, and support functions. The app uses Next.js API route handling to expose backend logic through URLs.\par\par\b 9. Data Table and Search Pattern\b0\par The hook src/hooks/useDataTable.ts is a reusable pattern for managing search, sorting, and pagination.\par\par Concepts involved: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - search filtering by text fields\par - sort toggle by field name\par - pagination with page size and total pages\par - start and end index calculation\par - filtering and sorted result generation\par\pard\par This hook is used across dashboard, employees, tasks, leave, attendance, reports, holidays, and others for consistent table behavior.\par\par\b 10. Employee Management\b0\par The employee module stores details like name, email, department, designation, joining date, mobile, salary, status, and avatar.\par\par It supports: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - adding new employees\par - updating data\par - deleting employees\par - viewing employee details\par - employee-specific dashboards\par\pard\par This is the foundation of the HR system because most other modules are related to employees.\par\par\b 11. Attendance System\b0\par Attendance is tracked by session records that capture login and logout events. This project stores attendance with fields such as date, loginTime, logoutTime, workingHours, status, productivity, and session histories.\par\par Key concepts: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - login and logout tracking\par - total working duration calculation\par - presence or absence status\par - productivity score\par - attendance history for each employee\par\pard\par This helps management monitor whether employees are working on time and how productive they are.\par\par\b 12. Task Management\b0\par Tasks are assigned to employees with priority, status, date ranges, comments, and review outcome.\par\par Task lifecycle: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - assigned\par - in progress\par - completed\par - reviewed\par\pard\par HR can review and rate the performance of submitted tasks. This creates a workflow for work monitoring and performance management.\par\par\b 13. Leave Management\b0\par Leave requests include type, reason, start date, end date, total days, and review workflow.\par\par Leave statuses: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - pending\par - hr_approved\par - hr_rejected\par - admin_approved\par - admin_rejected\par - cancelled\par\pard\par This concept models the leave approval hierarchy where HR and admin review requests before final approval.\par\par\b 14. Expense Management\b0\par Employee expenses are stored and reviewed before reimbursement. Fields include category, amount, date, receipt URL, description, and status.\par\par Typical categories: travel, office supplies, client meetings, food, equipment, and other.\par\par This reflects a business process where employees submit expenses, HR reviews them, and admin approves or rejects reimbursement.\par\par\b 15. Holiday Management\b0\par The system can define public and special holidays. The Holiday schema contains name, type, start date, end date, and active status.\par\par Holiday types may include: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - company holiday\par - optional holiday\par - restricted holiday\par - custom holiday\par\pard\par This helps the organization keep a holiday calendar and align leave planning with official schedules.\par\par\b 16. Notifications and Alerts\b0\par Notifications are central to the system. They are sent for tasks, approvals, reimbursements, broadcasts, and reminders.\par\par Important concepts: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - recipient-based notifications\par - read/unread state\par - system broadcasts to many users\par - notification module and action URL links\par\pard\par The notification mechanism helps keep employees and HR aware of actions needing attention.\par\par\b 17. Payroll and Salary Slip Concepts\b0\par Payroll logic is defined in src/lib/payroll.ts and is one of the key business features.\par\par Concepts included: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - annual CTC and monthly CTC\par - basic salary and HRA\par - conveyance, medical allowance, special allowance\par - PF and ESI contribution\par - TDS and professional tax\par - LWP deduction\par - gross salary and net salary\par - amount in words conversion\par\pard\par The project computes earnings and deductions and generates salary slip data used in payslip creation. The SalarySlip model stores many values for each pay period.\par\par\b 18. PDF and Salary Slip Generation\b0\par The application includes PDF support for salary slips using PDFKit. Salary slip endpoints exist under src/app/api/salary-slips. This means the system can generate a payslip document for employee viewing or downloading.\par\par This is important for payroll documentation and employee financial reporting.\par\par\b 19. Cloudinary Image Upload\b0\par The profile page supports uploading a profile image. In src/app/actions.ts, uploadImageToCloudinary(base64Image) uploads the image to Cloudinary.\par\par This concept is used for: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - employee profile images\par - admin, HR, and employee avatars\par - visual identity in the system\par\pard\par This allows the HR platform to present a more human-centered interface.\par\par\b 20. Maintenance Mode\b0\par There is a maintenance mode concept used in the app layout. If maintenance mode is active, non-admin users are redirected to a maintenance page.\par\par This is a good operational feature for system updates, downtime, or changes in business workflows.\par\par\b 21. UI Design and Layout Concept\b0\par The interface uses a modern administrative dashboard design. Some main design ideas are: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - sidebar navigation\par - top header with profile and actions\par - card-based dashboard metrics\par - tables with sorting and pagination\par - forms with validation\par - alerts and toasts\par - role-based layout changes\par\pard\par The design follows an internal business dashboard model rather than a simple CRUD form layout.\par\par\b 22. Real-World Business Purpose\b0\par This project is not just a technical demo; it reflects a complete HR operations workflow. The main business goals are: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - track employees and their status\par - manage attendance and productivity\par - assign and monitor tasks\par - handle leave approvals\par - process employee expense claims\par - maintain company holidays\par - generate payroll and salary slips\par - notify employees about updates\par - provide reports for management decisions\par\pard\par\b 23. Summary\b0\par The project combines modern frontend architecture, database modeling, role-based access control, and HR workflow automation. The most important concepts are: \par\pard\li360\fi-360\tx360 - Next.js app architecture\par - role-based access control\par - MongoDB with Mongoose\par - server actions and API routes\par - UI state and search logic\par - payroll calculation and payslip generation\par - notifications and audit-style tracking\par - employee lifecycle and HR operations\par\pard\par This is a complete employee management dashboard with real-world business logic.\par\par\b 24. How to Use This Document\b0\par This RTF file can be opened in Word, Google Docs, or LibreOffice. From there, it can be saved as PDF or printed for presentation. If you want a formal report, add your name, organization, and date in Word and export it to PDF.\par\pard\par\b End of Document\b0\par}